WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:08.513
In this video, you will set up a contest exactly your way: your own voting categories, invited judges, a prize, and your own rules.

00:00:08.513 --> 00:00:12.815
I will explain every choice as we go, so you know what each one does.

00:00:12.815 --> 00:00:14.352
We will start on the map.

00:00:15.251 --> 00:00:19.313
To begin, open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:19.313 --> 00:00:21.438
That is the only address you need.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.707
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:26.707 --> 00:00:30.451
The first time you visit, it asks to use your location.

00:00:30.451 --> 00:00:31.788
Tap Use my location.

00:00:33.521 --> 00:00:37.958
That is how the map shows how far things are, and gives you directions.

00:00:37.958 --> 00:00:41.163
Your browser asks permission as well, so tap Allow.

00:00:41.163 --> 00:00:45.723
Your location is used only on your device, and you can say no at any time.

00:00:48.029 --> 00:00:49.809
The map zooms to where you are.

00:00:49.809 --> 00:00:53.981
There are no events on your street, so tap Show all of Southern California.

00:00:55.637 --> 00:01:00.394
Now every place shows how far away it is, nearest first, so you can plan your drive.

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:04.029
Now look at the top right corner of the map.

00:01:04.029 --> 00:01:05.225
See the three dots?

00:01:05.225 --> 00:01:09.527
That is the menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:01:09.527 --> 00:01:10.065
Tap them.

00:01:11.669 --> 00:01:12.932
In the menu, tap Add.

00:01:12.932 --> 00:01:17.238
That is where you add anything new: an event, a contest, or your own house.

00:01:18.927 --> 00:01:21.465
This is the Add page, with three choices.

00:01:21.465 --> 00:01:22.553
We want a contest.

00:01:23.353 --> 00:01:25.998
We are creating a contest, so tap A contest.

00:01:28.091 --> 00:01:31.651
I will type Pine Ridge Holiday Lights 2026.

00:01:31.651 --> 00:01:32.784
Then tap Next.

00:01:35.255 --> 00:01:36.563
Next, who is running it.

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:38.028
Type the name of your group.

00:01:39.686 --> 00:01:42.289
Then pick the city the homes are in, and tap Next.

00:01:44.348 --> 00:01:47.117
The welcome message is already written for you.

00:01:47.117 --> 00:01:49.482
Keep it, or change it to sound like you.

00:01:49.482 --> 00:01:50.002
Tap Next.

00:01:51.805 --> 00:01:56.445
A website is optional, and your contest goes live right away without one.

00:01:56.445 --> 00:01:57.010
Tap Next.

00:01:58.814 --> 00:02:04.397
These three dates are filled in for you: the last day to enter, and when voting starts and ends.

00:02:04.397 --> 00:02:04.915
Tap Next.

00:02:06.717 --> 00:02:08.209
Here is the big choice.

00:02:08.209 --> 00:02:10.696
Quick start sets everything up for you.

00:02:10.696 --> 00:02:14.239
Customize everything lets you decide each rule yourself.

00:02:14.239 --> 00:02:18.280
We want to decide, so choose Customize everything, then tap Next.

00:02:20.832 --> 00:02:22.476
Now the voting categories.

00:02:22.476 --> 00:02:27.774
Every home competes in every category, and each voter picks one favorite home in each.

00:02:27.774 --> 00:02:30.880
So the categories are the awards you will give out.

00:02:31.581 --> 00:02:33.196
These four are suggested.

00:02:33.196 --> 00:02:34.687
Tap one to turn it off.

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:39.345
Best Overall is a category like any other, so you can keep it, or drop it.

00:02:39.345 --> 00:02:40.712
You need at least one.

00:02:41.412 --> 00:02:42.813
You can add your own.

00:02:42.813 --> 00:02:45.870
Type a name, like Best Inflatable, and tap Add.

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:49.118
Funny, local categories are a big part of the fun.

00:02:49.118 --> 00:02:50.009
Then tap Next.

00:02:52.001 --> 00:02:53.447
Next, who gets to vote.

00:02:53.447 --> 00:02:54.954
There are three choices.

00:02:54.954 --> 00:02:58.689
Everyone means anyone with an account, one vote per category.

00:02:58.689 --> 00:03:00.919
That award is called People's Choice.

00:03:01.621 --> 00:03:04.948
Judges only means just the people you invite can vote.

00:03:04.948 --> 00:03:07.125
That award is called Judges' Choice.

00:03:07.828 --> 00:03:10.029
And Everyone and judges does both.

00:03:10.029 --> 00:03:18.391
The public and your judges vote separately, so every category has two winners, one chosen by the neighborhood and one by the judges.

00:03:18.391 --> 00:03:20.843
Judges do not vote in the public vote.

00:03:20.843 --> 00:03:23.295
We will choose that one, then tap Next.

00:03:25.798 --> 00:03:26.871
Now your judges.

00:03:26.871 --> 00:03:29.207
Type one email address on each line.

00:03:29.207 --> 00:03:34.636
Each judge gets an invitation with a private link, and signs in with that same email.

00:03:34.636 --> 00:03:41.328
Choose people your neighbors will trust, like a city staff member, a teacher, or a local lighting company.

00:03:42.028 --> 00:03:43.031
I will add two.

00:03:43.031 --> 00:03:47.863
You can add or remove judges later from your dashboard, so nothing is final.

00:03:47.863 --> 00:03:48.428
Tap Next.

00:03:50.201 --> 00:03:51.426
How do judges vote?

00:03:51.426 --> 00:03:53.692
Pick a favorite is simple and quick.

00:03:53.692 --> 00:03:58.286
Each judge chooses one home in each category, the same way the public does.

00:03:58.988 --> 00:04:01.481
Score every home is for formal judging.

00:04:01.481 --> 00:04:07.839
Each judge gives every home a score from one to ten, in every category, and the highest average wins.

00:04:07.839 --> 00:04:15.880
With five or more judges, the highest and lowest score for each home are dropped, so one unusual judge cannot decide the result.

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:18.124
We will choose score, then tap Next.

00:04:20.637 --> 00:04:22.713
How should new entries be approved?

00:04:22.713 --> 00:04:25.771
I review each entry first is the recommended choice.

00:04:25.771 --> 00:04:31.367
Nothing appears on the map until you approve it, so you can screen out photos that do not belong.

00:04:32.069 --> 00:04:36.607
Publish entries right away is faster, but you cannot screen photos first.

00:04:36.607 --> 00:04:38.877
We will keep the recommended choice.

00:04:38.877 --> 00:04:39.429
Tap Next.

00:04:41.154 --> 00:04:44.442
Should people see the vote counts while voting is open?

00:04:44.442 --> 00:04:47.672
Hiding them until you announce winners is recommended.

00:04:47.672 --> 00:04:51.842
It stops bandwagon voting, where people just vote for whoever is ahead.

00:04:52.543 --> 00:04:56.917
Showing running totals builds excitement, but everyone can see who is ahead.

00:04:56.917 --> 00:04:59.984
You always see the counts yourself on your dashboard.

00:04:59.984 --> 00:05:02.313
Keep the recommended choice and tap Next.

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:05.445
A few fairness rules.

00:05:05.445 --> 00:05:09.404
The first is whether one home can win more than one category.

00:05:09.404 --> 00:05:13.874
By default it can, because the best home in each category simply wins.

00:05:14.577 --> 00:05:20.927
One win per home spreads the awards around, so a home that wins one category cannot win a later one.

00:05:20.927 --> 00:05:31.677
Below, you can see what is already protected for you: one vote per person per category, tied to a verified email, nobody can vote for their own home, and ties are shared.

00:05:31.677 --> 00:05:33.563
Keep the default and tap Next.

00:05:35.291 --> 00:05:36.367
Is there a prize?

00:05:36.367 --> 00:05:37.444
This is optional.

00:05:37.444 --> 00:05:42.468
A prize is shown on your contest page, and with the winners when you announce them.

00:05:42.468 --> 00:05:45.637
No prize still gives winners a crown and recognition.

00:05:46.338 --> 00:05:50.818
You can give the same prize to every winner, or a different prize for each award.

00:05:50.818 --> 00:05:53.058
We will choose one prize for all winners.

00:05:54.708 --> 00:05:57.884
Describe it, for example, a fifty dollar gift card.

00:05:57.884 --> 00:06:01.853
If a local business is providing it, you can name them here too.

00:06:01.853 --> 00:06:02.708
Then tap Next.

00:06:04.432 --> 00:06:06.230
These are your official rules.

00:06:06.230 --> 00:06:10.581
We drafted them for you, and people have to accept them before they enter.

00:06:10.581 --> 00:06:15.163
They cover who can enter, how winners are chosen, and what the prize terms are.

00:06:15.862 --> 00:06:17.212
You can edit anything.

00:06:17.212 --> 00:06:21.201
If you offer a prize, it is a good idea to have a lawyer read them.

00:06:21.201 --> 00:06:21.729
Tap Next.

00:06:23.456 --> 00:06:24.681
Last is the review.

00:06:24.681 --> 00:06:30.441
Everything you chose is listed here, and each line has an Edit link if you want to change it.

00:06:30.441 --> 00:06:33.444
Your first contest in a 12-month window is free.

00:06:33.444 --> 00:06:37.365
If you run more, you choose a pass first: see the Pricing page.

00:06:37.365 --> 00:06:40.245
Nothing is public until you tap Create contest.

00:06:40.948 --> 00:06:43.401
When you are happy with it, tap Create contest.

00:06:45.877 --> 00:06:47.223
Your contest is live.

00:06:47.223 --> 00:06:49.550
This page explains what happens next.

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:57.202
Share your link, neighbors enter, you approve the entries, the community and your judges vote, and you announce the winners.

00:06:57.202 --> 00:06:58.549
Tap Open my dashboard.

00:07:00.484 --> 00:07:06.132
This is your dashboard, where you run the contest, with your link and QR code ready to share.

00:07:06.132 --> 00:07:07.695
Sharing is the next video.

00:07:08.896 --> 00:07:10.645
Next up: Share your contest.
